## #13 · `scripts/generateRegistry.mjs`

```diff
 function escapeCell(value) {
-  return String(value).replace(/\|/g, '\\|')
+  // (?<!\\) so an already-escaped pipe is left alone. Without it, running escapeCell over
+  // previously-escaped text doubles the backslash and the cell renders a literal "\|".
+  return String(value).replace(/(?<!\\)\|/g, '\\|')
 }
```

Plus a regression case. There's no test file for the generator today, so this creates one:

```diff
+ scripts/generateRegistry.test.mjs   (new)
```

```js
// escapeCell is the only pure, self-contained function in the generator, and it guards
// table integrity — an unescaped pipe shifts every column after it.
describe('escapeCell', () => {
  test('escapes a bare pipe', …)                    // 'a' | 'b'  →  'a' \| 'b'
  test('leaves an already-escaped pipe alone', …)    // a \| b     →  a \| b
  test('handles a mix', …)                           // a \| b | c →  a \| b \| c
  test('passes text with no pipes through', …)
});
```

⚠️ **Caveat:** `escapeCell` isn't exported, and `generateRegistry.mjs` runs its whole scan on import. Testing it needs either exporting the function or duplicating it in the test. I'd **export it** — one line, and it makes the guard testable. Tell me if you'd rather not touch the export surface.

## #12 · `overrides/app/theme/fontFace.test.tsx` (new)

No change to `fontFace.tsx` itself — CodeRabbit asked for coverage through the CSS output, not the private helpers.

```js
// assetRoot resolved the wrong path once already: fonts were served as HTML because the
